  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e9620f8c34305754d8cc9a7e49e852d9, type: 3}
  m_Name: QIMG_en
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_LocaleId:
    m_Code: en
  m_SharedData: {fileID: 11400000, guid: efcebb6c42e8bae4c89fe410ca19cc7e, type: 2}
  m_Metadata:
    m_Items: []
  m_TableData:
  - m_Id: 3550279766016
    m_Localized: During dental surgery to extract lower third molars, a 58-year-old
      male patient experienced an episode of intense coughing followed by dyspnea.
      A fragment of a tooth was
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 3552171397120
    m_Localized: aspirated during the procedure, but the event went unnoticed at
      the time. Three days later, the patient was admitted to the emergency room
      with fever, chest pain, and difficulty breathing. Physical examination revealed
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 3553526157312
    m_Localized: rales (abnormal breath sounds) in the right hemithorax, and a chest
      X-ray showed a pulmonary infiltrate suggestive of lobar pneumonia. Bronchoscopy
      confirmed the presence of
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 3554918666240
    m_Localized: A tooth fragment impacted in a right lower segmental bronchus. The
      patient received antibiotic treatment, and the foreign body was removed. Based
      on this context, which organ was most threatened and had its functions compromised?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7461640212480
    m_Localized: A 17-year-old boy was admitted to the emergency room after falling
      during a soccer match. According to reports, the patient fell chin-first to
      the ground after being pushed, hitting his lower face. He arrived complaining
      of severe jaw pain and oral bleeding.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7461665378304
    m_Localized: He also had swelling in the chin region and difficulty speaking.
      Clinical and radiographic examination revealed a fracture of tooth 31 (lower
      left central incisor) and a fracture in the left mandibular body, with slight
      deviation of the dental arch.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7461665378305
    m_Localized: The patient was referred for joint evaluation by dentistry and oral
      and maxillofacial surgery. Given this context, which anatomical structure is
      associated with this type of injury?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7461669572608
    m_Localized: A 27-year-old female patient presented to the emergency room with
      persistent fever, fatigue, chills, and muscle aches for about 10 days. During
      the medical history, she reported that
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7461669572609
    m_Localized: had recently undergone a dental procedure to treat deep cavities
      in two lower molars, but did not follow the instructions to complete the prescribed
      course of antibiotics.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7461669572610
    m_Localized: On physical examination, he had a heart murmur and small red lesions
      on the tips of his fingers (Janeway lesions). An echocardiogram revealed vegetations
      attached to the mitral valve, confirming the diagnosis of infective endocarditis.
      Which anatomical structure was affected by this condition?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7461669572611
    m_Localized: A 70-year-old patient presents with recurrent episodes of sudden
      weakness on the right side of the body and difficulty speaking that last about
      10 minutes and resolve spontaneously.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7461669572612
    m_Localized: "Doppler ultrasound reveals critical stenosis (obstruction) of the
      left internal carotid artery. Which organ is directly affected by this condition?\r"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  references:
    version: 2
    RefIds: []
